  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-131522",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-2.1<Z<-1.03).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/97b441bbce686653a8d95dc7190f03390b52099223de3ab40c83831564118a28.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.1<Z<-1.03) & =P(Z<-1.03)-P(Z\\le -2.1) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.03)-P(Z\\le -2.1) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.03)-Φ(-2.1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.1) & =0.0179 \\\\ Φ(-1.03) & =0.1515\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.1<Z<-1.03) & =Φ(-1.03)-Φ(-2.1) \\\\  & =0.1515-0.0179 \\\\  & =0.1336.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
